exports[`every prompt the game paints with > walkers standing and walking, every way > the four ways on one sheet 1`] = `
"Stylised low-poly isometric fantasy game art, light-neutral.
Flat faceted shapes built from a few large flat planes with crisp hard edges, like cut paper or a clean vector illustration.
NO LIGHTING AT ALL: every material is one single flat base colour on all its facets, with no lit side, no shadow side, no highlights, no gradients and no glow; facets are shown only by a very thin, slightly darker seam where two planes meet. No outlines, no texture, no noise.
A small harmonious palette of soft, muted warm pastels (sand, terracotta, dusty rose, sage green, teal, cream, brass). No writing anywhere.
Paint Mara from the reference image alone, four times side by side in one row, full body, standing in a relaxed pose, all four the same size and standing on the same line, evenly spaced with wide empty gaps so no two touch. From left to right:
1. in a three-quarter view from the front, facing the LOWER-LEFT corner of the picture: the nose, chest and toes point towards the viewer's left, exactly halfway between facing the viewer and a profile facing the left edge of the picture; their LEFT shoulder is nearer to us and their right shoulder further away.
2. in a three-quarter view from the front, facing the LOWER-RIGHT corner of the picture: the nose, chest and toes point towards the viewer's right, exactly halfway between facing the viewer and a profile facing the right edge of the picture; their RIGHT shoulder is nearer to us and their left shoulder further away.
3. in a three-quarter view from behind, facing the UPPER-LEFT corner of the picture: turned away from us and towards the viewer's left, exactly halfway between seen from behind and a profile facing the left edge of the picture; we see their back and the back of the head, the face hidden; their LEFT shoulder is nearer to us.
4. in a three-quarter view from behind, facing the UPPER-RIGHT corner of the picture: turned away from us and towards the viewer's right, exactly halfway between seen from behind and a profile facing the right edge of the picture; we see their back and the back of the head, the face hidden; their RIGHT shoulder is nearer to us.
All four are the same Mara: copy exactly how they look in the reference (face, hair, clothes, colours, proportions and what they carry), the same in every view; only the way they face changes.
Paint them in the style described above, even where the reference images are painted in another style.
Background: one flat pure magenta (#FF00FF) behind all four, with no floor, shadow, labels or numbers. No magenta in the character.
